{"title":"Germany fact of the day","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/914712770/0/marginalrevolution~Germany-fact-of-the-day.html","date":1741850542000,"content":"<blockquote><p>Germany opened its doors a decade ago to nearly 1 million Syrians, taking in more than any other country in Europe. Today, some 6,000 Syrian doctors make up the single largest group of foreign-born physicians, filling vital gaps in care at hospitals and clinics from the Alps to the Baltic Sea. That is especially true in rural areas, where attracting doctors can be hard. But even in big cities, Syrian doctors now make up the majority of attending physicians at some medical practices.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2025/03/11/germany-syrian-doctors-refugees/\" target=\"_blank\">more from The Washington Post</a>.  Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/02/grok-3-on-the-syrians-in-germany.html\" target=\"_blank\">my previous post on Syrians in Germany</a>.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/03/germany-fact-of-the-day-14.html\">Germany fact of the day</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/914712770/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/914712770/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/914712770/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/914712770/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"2